<%# locals: (agreement_partial:, minor:, guardian:, minor_label: nil) %>
<%# Fuime: the agreement a guardian reads and the box they tick, shared by the
    two screens that can produce a signature — guardianships/show (a parent
    following a teen's emailed invite) and the family setup wizard's `sign`
    step (a parent setting the family up themselves).

    Extracted byte-for-byte from guardianships/show. The checkbox id, the label
    wording and the scroll box are what specs and, more importantly, what past
    signers saw; they must not drift between the two entry points, because the
    consent record does not say which screen produced it.

    The FORM is deliberately not in here. The two callers post to different
    URLs (an invite token vs the wizard step) and the wizard's version has a
    name field above the box, so the wrapper, the submit button and the
    record-keeping note stay with the caller. What is shared is the text and
    the tick. %>
<% label_name = local_assigns[:minor_label].presence || minor&.name.presence || "this minor" %>

<h2 class="mb-2 mt-4">Guardian agreement</h2>
<div class="border rounded-lg p-4 mb-4 overflow-y-auto wizard-agreement" style="max-height: 24rem">
  <% if agreement_partial %>
    <%= render agreement_partial, minor: minor, guardian: guardian %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="error mb-0">
      The agreement text could not be loaded. Please contact
      <%= mail_to "support@fuime.com" %> before signing.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<div class="field field--checkbox mb-3" style="align-items: flex-start;">
  <%= check_box_tag :agree, "1", false,
                    required: true,
                    id: "agree",
                    class: "mt1",
                    style: "width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem; flex-shrink: 0;",
                    aria: { required: true } %>
  <%= label_tag :agree do %>
    I confirm I am the parent or legal guardian of
    <strong><%= label_name %></strong>,
    that I am 18 or older, and I agree to the guardian agreement above.
  <% end %>
</div>
